  "notes": "USAGE:\nストック typically refers to keeping a reserve of consumable items (food, supplies, etc.) rather than financial stocks (which is {株|かぶ} in Japanese). ストックする functions as a suru-verb meaning 'to stock up' or 'to keep in reserve.'\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ストックする: to stock up, to keep in reserve\n- ストックが{切|き}れる: to run out of stock\n- ストックがある: to have stock on hand\n- {食料|しょくりょう}のストック: food reserves\n- {在庫|ざいこ}ストック: inventory stock",
